{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_functions_fn_add_po_delivery_fn_add_po_delivery", "label": "fn_add_po_delivery", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_add_po_delivery.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Card ^ref-19 / D01: one dispatch round and its lot are one write, in one transaction, so a lot can never be orphaned from a round (lots.po_delivery_id is NOT NULL UNIQUE and there deliberately is no fn_create_lot). Enforces R4 idempotency (client-generated key; a replay returns the same lot id), BR03/R16/ADR-011 (foodiva_sent_weight_kg is frozen onto the lot as the yield divisor), BR11 (the lot must land at a CHEF_HOUSE location, never BRANCH or CENTRAL), and the PO over-delivery guard under `select ... for update` on purchase_orders so two concurrent 60 kg rounds cannot both commit against a 100 kg PO. Boundary is `>` not `>=` \u2014 cumulative exactly equal to ordered is a fully delivered PO. seq is derived under the lock, never a parameter, because round order drives v_po_outstanding and every FIFO view. Touches no stock_ledger row: a booked round is a plan, not a movement."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_functions_fn_add_po_delivery_fn_add_po_delivery", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_require_owner_fn_require_owner", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_add_po_delivery.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_add_po_delivery_fn_add_po_delivery", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_locations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_add_po_delivery.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_add_po_delivery_fn_add_po_delivery", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000003_purchasing_production_po_deliveries",